===== AGENTS.md =====
# AGENTS.md

Guidance for AI coding agents working in **fixture**.

## Stack

- Language: TypeScript (strict)
- Module format: ESM
- Package manager: npm
- Bundler: tsup
- Tests: vitest
- Lint/format: eslint-prettier

## Commands

- Type-check: `npm run typecheck`
- Lint: `npm run lint`
- Test: `npm test`
- Build: `npm run build`

## Conventions

- Source lives in `src/`. Keep the public API in `src/index.ts`.
- Add or update tests for any behavior change.
- Prefer explicit types on exported functions; keep `strict` passing.
- Do not commit `dist/` or `node_modules/`.

===== CLAUDE.md =====
See [AGENTS.md](./AGENTS.md) for build/test commands and conventions.

===== CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md =====
# Code of Conduct

This project follows the [Contributor Covenant](https://www.contributor-covenant.org/version/2/1/code_of_conduct/).
By participating, you are expected to uphold this code. Report unacceptable
behavior to the maintainers.

===== CONTRIBUTING.md =====
# Contributing

Thanks for your interest in contributing!

## Development

```sh
npm install
npm test
```

## Pull requests

- Create a branch, make your change, and open a PR against `main`.
- Make sure lint, types and tests pass.


===== Dockerfile =====
# A worker is a long-running process, NOT an HTTP server — so there is no EXPOSE
# and no HTTP HEALTHCHECK; liveness is the process. STOPSIGNAL makes `docker stop`
# send SIGTERM so the worker drains in-flight work before exiting.
# --- build stage ---
FROM node:24-slim AS build
WORKDIR /app
COPY package*.json ./
RUN npm ci
COPY . .
RUN npm run build

# --- deps stage: production-only node_modules ---
FROM node:24-slim AS deps
WORKDIR /app
COPY package*.json ./
RUN npm ci --omit=dev

# --- runtime stage: slim, non-root ---
FROM node:24-slim
WORKDIR /app
ENV NODE_ENV=production
COPY --from=deps /app/node_modules ./node_modules
COPY --from=build /app/dist ./dist
COPY package.json ./
USER node
STOPSIGNAL SIGTERM
CMD ["node", "dist/index.js"]

